    "result": "I implemented `RateLimiter` in `solution.py` and wrote a 59-test pytest suite in `tests/test_solution.py`; `python -m pytest -q tests` passes. Each client keeps a deque of `(time, cost)` records, and expired records (`now - t >= window_seconds`) are dropped on every call. `allow` checks the cost and then records the request only if it fits. `remaining` and `retry_after` only read state. A shared latest-time value rejects any `now` that goes backwards, across all clients and methods. Invalid `limit`, `window_seconds` or `cost` raise `ValueError`, and `bool` is rejected wherever an integer is expected. `retry_after` returns the wait until enough of the oldest records expire to fit the requested cost. I did not run coverage, CRAP, mutation or bandit checks, since only the test command was permitted. The tests cover the boundaries and the failure cases, but I have not measured their strength against those gates.",
